This package is a standalone port of dsh-at-file by omdsh-dev, used under the
MIT License. The original project lives at:

    https://github.com/omdsh-dev/dsh-at-file

Upstream ships TypeScript sources, so this is a port rather than a repackage.
The behaviour is unchanged — the @ picker, the workspace index walk, the
filter settings, and the pre-step <workspace-reference> marker all work as
upstream designed them. The differences are packaging and this repository's
conventions:

  - Renamed to @dsh-pro/at-file, and the Typert identities follow. Upstream
    keys its manifest, invocation ids, and type symbols under the package name
    `dsh-at-file`; the registry rejects duplicate package-face keys and
    duplicate invocation ids, so a fork that kept them could not be installed
    beside the original. Host and client both build from src/contract.ts, so
    the two halves cannot drift apart. The one identity left alone is
    `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session/types#SessionId`: it must equal the agent lookup
    provider's wire identity, and it is not ours to rename.

  - The client bundle's __ModuleLoader__ id is the installed package name,
    because the web boot manifest looks a bundle up by that name.

  - English only. Upstream carries a Simplified Chinese dictionary as the
    key-set source of truth with English mirroring it. This repository writes
    English only, so the English dictionary is now the source of truth and is
    registered under both locale ids — selecting Chinese leaves the harness in
    Chinese and these panels in English, rather than rendering raw message
    keys from an unregistered namespace.

  - schemastery and zod are bundled rather than installed. The harness profile
    resolves only what it ships itself.

  - The ./invariant companion is dropped. It registers a no-op installer to
    reserve package ownership in the diagnostics registry, and its own
    docstring records that the package has no runtime invariant to assert.

  - dsh.plugin.json and README.zh.md are dropped: the first is read by
    `dsh plugin add`, which this repository does not use, and the second is a
    translation this repository does not carry.

  - Type-checking resolves the harness differently. The client half imports
    harness client packages for the module augmentations that declare the
    composer slot names it fills; upstream resolves them with `link:`
    devDependencies into a sibling deepseek-harness monorepo checkout, which
    this repository does not have. Installing them from npm does not work
    either: the published rc.7 packages peer `^0.1.0-rc.7`, npm resolves that
    to rc.8, and rc.8 peers `^0.1.0-rc.8`, so the graph has no solution.
    Instead scripts/link-harness.mjs symlinks the INSTALLED harness into
    node_modules before tsc runs, so the types can never drift from the
    deployment — they are the deployment.

